                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I wish I could leave a positive review but... First the positives. The first three episodes are great. The gameplay is a little slow but it's unique mechanic is awesome. The story is engrossing. However it does rely pretty heavily on finding random bit of lore scattered around to get the full effect. \r\n\r\n*Slight Spoiler*\r\n\r\nThe negatives are unfortunately too glaring for me personally. After episode three you are stripped of your abilities and have to go back to playing like the beginning again. The one new mechanic, photo mode, is bland and awkward compared to previous abilities. The story, which up until this point was on a steady climb, seems to take sudden dive and slows way down. These changes were too much for me and I could not bring myself to finish episode 4.",
